    904  f0fe							;   and jumps into .Line), so a pushed return
    905  f0fe							;   address would leak 2 bytes every frame.
    906  f0fe							;   Its early-out jumps back to .RowNoSlot1.
    907  f0fe				   Slot1Keep
    908  f0fe							; (2026-10-15) GRP0 blank REMOVED: +5c pushed the rows0/1 setup
    909  f0fe							; segment to 75c armed (>=74 = write lands next line = +1 stall line
    910  f0fe							; = whole-screen shift). The blank only traded a stale-byte duplicate
    911  f0fe							; for a blank line at band boundaries — shipped pre-99b8e86 without
    912  f0fe							; either; case15 filters zero writes so the Y-align guard is unaffected.
    913  f0fe							; --- Scanlines this pass (N=4): bands 0-2 = 36; band 3 = 24+off (tide,
    914  f0fe							; CollisionX). The bottom water strip (last 12-off lines,
    915  f0fe							; bottom_band_plan rule 2) renders in .WaterRow after this pass — its own
    916  f0fe							; setup line + (12-off) bodies, so the bottom band spans 38 picture lines
    917  f0fe							; and the cave body count is exactly CAVE_LINES (144).
    918  f0fe							; Split tail (2026-10-05, row1 setup gap 77->74): the non-bottom gate used
    919  f0fe							; to pay `bne` 3c to skip the tide load AND share the WSYNC — gap was 77
    920  f0fe							; (stall, +1 line/frame). Non-bottom bands now store+WSYNC before the tide
    921  f0fe							; block, then jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line =
    922  f0fe							; 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC = 72 <=76). Bottom-band path byte-identical in cost
    923  f0fe							; (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    924  f0fe							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    925  f0fe							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
    926  f0fe							; A1 gap fix (2026-10-05): `sta Temp` (+3c in .Row) pushed gaps to
    927  f0fe							; 77/79 = stall EVERY frame (265-line frames). `sta LineCount` moved
    928  f0fe							; AFTER `sta WSYNC` — same bytes, -3c from the gap window, +3c to the
    929  f0fe							; first body line (66max+3LC[+3jmp]+3WSYNC = 75 rows0/1, 72 row2).
    930  f0fe							; LineCount is not read until the line's `dec` tail — the early store
    931  f0fe							; was never required; keep the store strictly between WSYNC and .Line.
    932  f0fe		       e0 03		      cpx	#TILE_ROWS-1
    933  f100		       f0 09		      beq	.RowLinesTide	; bottom band: tide count (24+off) from CollisionX
